{"_data": [{"contents": [{"type": "lesson_name", "content": ""}, {"type": "unit_name", "content": "Operating Systems"}, {"type": "position", "content": 5}, {"type": "origin", "content": "stub"}, {"type": "lesson", "content": 2}, {"type": "level", "content": "A1.1"}], "type": "metadata"}, {"contents": [{"type": "test", "content": "false"}], "type": "achievment_test"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "These are words you use to talk about operating systems"}], "type": "target_word_describer"}, {"contents": [{"type": "primary", "content": "Understands systems theories, business processes and basic concepts on IT.  Create a map of processes that allows identifying areas in an information system, using IT tools to generate reports based on the company's needs."}, {"type": "secondary_1", "content": "Understands simple information in slow conversations about the communicative topics and vocabulary related to this level.  Recognizes basic ideas on IT concepts, systems theory, and diagrams of processes."}], "type": "objectives"}, {"type": "background_image", "content": "enpe8n1le02ob05re1img01.jpg"}, {"contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Simple Connectors"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "A <span class=\"italic\">connector</span> is used to create connections between words and clauses. When you use them to join sentences, you give equal emphasis to these sentences you connect."}, {"type": "text", "content": "<span class=\"strong\">And, but, nor, yet</span> and <span class=\"strong\">or</span> are simple <span class= \"strong\">connectors</span> or conjunctions. <br> <br> In this object, you are going to focus on the uses of <span class= \"strong\"> and </span>.<br><br>  <span class= \"strong\">And </span>  is a connector </span>  or a linking word that joins two words, ideas, or phrases together. <br><br>  Example: <br> \u2022\t<span class= \"italic\"> I want a word processor <span class= \"strong\">and </span> a spreadsheet in my computer. <br> \u2022\tHe went to the store <span class= \"strong\">and </span>  bought a computer. </span>"}, {"type": "example", "content": "The Operating System was developed to control programs and applications in a computer."}, {"type": "example", "content": "The control-card interpreter reads and carries all the commands when you point or use the \"enter\" key on the keyboard."}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Operating System: Types"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "The most commonly used types of operating systems are Batch Operating System, Time-sharing Operating System, Distributed Operating System, Network Operating System, and Real-Time Operating System."}, {"type": "text", "content": "<ul>  <li>The Batch Operating System is an OS in which users create their job in an off-line device and which then submits the device to the computer. The problem is that it makes the computer slow. </li><br><br>  <li>The Time-sharing Operating System is a way to work in which many people use the same software at the same time. In Time-Sharing Systems, the objective is to minimize response time. </li><br><br>  <li>The Distributed Operating System uses multiple CPU to help multiple real-time applications and users. The different tasks are distributed among the processors accordingly. </li><br><br>  <li>Network Operating Systems run on a server and offer the server the skill to manage data, users, groups, security, applications, and other networking functions. Examples of network operating systems include Microsoft Windows Server 2003, Microsoft Windows Server 2008, UNIX, Linux, Mac OS X, Novell NetWare, and BSD. </li> <br><br>  <li>The Real-Time Operating System is similar to a data processing system in which the time interval required to process and respond to inputs is so small that it controls the environment. There are two types, one called hard real-time systems which complete difficult tasks on time and the soft real-time systems which are less restrictive. </li> </ul>"}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "automatically"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "when something occurs involuntarily, immediately, or very fast"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adverb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: This OS is just another program that can control automatically one task."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n1le02ob05aud01"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "transfer"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to move or take from one place to another\t"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: This OS is just another program that can control automatically one task and transfer data or information to another."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n1le02ob05aud02"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "point "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to show or aim at something or someone in the horizon, on a screen, places, or a document\t"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: For example, the control-card interpreter reads and carries all the commands when you point or use the \"enter\" key on the keyboard."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n1le02ob05aud03"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "rename "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to change the name of a person, animal, or thing"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: For example, you want to rename or change the name of a document."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n1le02ob05aud04"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "execute"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to do or develop an idea, job or order\t"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: you will introduce a command and this will be executed by the OS."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n1le02ob05aud05"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "Find information about operating systems and its parts."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Make a chart including what each part of the OS manages."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Present your chart to the class."}], "type": "takeaway_extension"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "I find information about operating systems and its parts."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I understand what each part of the OS manages."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I explain my ideas to the class."}], "type": "takeaway_assessment"}], "type": "sena", "labs": [{"stimuli": [{"template_override": 1, "type": "welcome", "_data": [], "contents": [{}], "id": 0}, {"_data": [], "title": "", "type": "audio", "template_override": 1, "id": 1, "contents": [{"value": {"audiosrc": "enpe8n1le02ob05re2aud01", "images": [{"time": "0", "image": "enpe8n1le02ob05re2img01.jpg", "id": 0, "text": "<div align=\"justify\">Go to page 50 in your books, please. The Operating System or OS controls programs and applications in a computer. It performs many functions to run all the tasks inside a computer. This OS is just another program that can control automatically one task and transfer data or information to another. In other words, it manages the computer hardware.</div>"}, {"time": "25000", "image": "enpe8n1le02ob05re2img02.jpg", "id": 1, "text": "<div align=\"justify\">At the beginning, programmers had to type the commands in order to perform a task. This took a lot of time and energy. Later, with the development of Operating System programs, the commands were easier to instruct. There are different types of OS like Batch Operating System, Time-sharing Operating Systems, Distributed Operating System, Network Operating System, and Real-Time Operating System.</div>"}, {"time": "53000", "image": "enpe8n1le02ob05re2img03.jpg", "id": 2, "text": "<div align=\"justify\">Let me show you how it works. When you turn on your computer, the OS starts and controls all the applications you need to perform a certain task. For example, the control-card interpreter reads and carries all the commands when you click the \"enter\" key on the keyboard. Then, the loader will run all the applications and programs that you want to use. Finally, the drivers or device driver will check and operate all the input devices and output devices. <br><br>As you can see, the user interacts with the OS to instruct a command. For example, you want to rename or change the name of a document. In order to do that, you will introduce a command and this will be executed by the OS. <br><br>Ok, now, let's turn the page and take a look at the description of each of these Operating Systems.</div>"}], "coverimg": "enpe8n1le02ob05re2img01.jpg"}, "type": "slideshow"}]}], "exercises": [{"stimuli_ids": [0], "_data": [{"contents": [{"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": "I can talk about the concept of operating system."}, {"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": "I can describe the operating system parts."}, {"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": "I can briefly explain the different types of operating systems."}, {"type": "Free Header Item", "content": "Do you believe that the Operating System is the most important component of a computer? Why? Why not?"}, {"type": "Free Header Item", "content": "Why do you think it is possible to work on different programs in a computer at the same time without them interfering with each other?"}], "type": "instructions"}, {"contents": [{"type": "group_name", "content": "Welcome"}], "type": "group"}, {"type": "feedback", "content": {"attempt_feedback": [{"type": "text", "content": "You have 2 tries"}, {"type": "text", "content": "you have 1 attempt left"}], "correct_feedback": "Correct", "incorrect_feedback": [{"type": "text", "content": "try again"}, {"type": "text", "content": "Maybe next time"}], "allowed_attempts": 2}}